[556.042358, "o", "\r\u001b[2d\u001b[37m\u001b[40mGulliver's Travels, Chapter One, A Voyage to Lilliput\r\u001b[4d\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mW\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mhen I awaked it was just daylight.  I attempted to rise, but I\r\u001b[5dfound my arms and legs were strongly fastened on each side to\r\u001b[6dthe ground; and my hair, which was long and thick, tied to the\r\u001b[7dground in the same manner.  I likewise felt several slender\r\u001b[8dligatures across my body, from my armpits to my thighs.  I\r\u001b[9dcould only look upward; the sun began to grow hot, and the\r\u001b[10dlight offended my eyes.  I heard a confused noise about me;\r\u001b[11dbut in the posture I lay could see nothing except the sky.  In a\r\u001b[12dlittle time I felt something alive moving on my left leg,\r\u001b[13dwhich, advancing gently forward over my breast, came almost up\r\u001b[14dto my chin; when bending my eyes downward as much as I could, I\r\u001b[15dperceived it to be a human creature not six inches high, with a\r\u001b[16dbow and arrow in his hands, and a quiver at his back.  In the\r\u001b[17dmean time I felt at least forty more of the same kind (as I\r\u001b[18dconjectured) following the first.\u001b[K\r\u001b[19d\u001b[K\u001b[31d\u001b[K\u001b[32d\u001b[K\u001b[33d\u001b[K\u001b[35;98H\u001b[1K \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mSpeed test\r\u001b[4dW\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[35;110H"]
