[699.240348, "o", "\r\u001b[2d\u001b[37m\u001b[40mTreasure Island, Chapter IV, \"The Sea Chest\", by Stevenson.\r\u001b[4d\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mI\u001b(B\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m lost no time, of course, in telling my mother all that\u001b[K\r\u001b[5dI knew, and perhaps should have told her long before,\u001b[K\r\u001b[6dand we saw ourselves at once in a difficult and dangerous\u001b[K\r\u001b[7dposition.  Some of the man's money--if he had any--was\u001b[K\r\u001b[8dcertainly due to us; but it was not likely that our\u001b[K\r\u001b[9dc"]
[699.24104, "o", "aptain's shipmates, above all the two specimens seen by\u001b[K\r\u001b[10dme, Black Dog and the blind beggar, would be inclined to\u001b[K\r\u001b[11dgive up their booty in payment of the dead man's debts.\u001b[K\r\u001b[12dThe captain's order to mount at once and ride for Dr.\u001b[K\r\u001b[13dLivesey would have left my mother alone and unprotected,\u001b[K\r\u001b[14dwhich was not to be thought of.  Indeed, it seemed\u001b[K\r\u001b[15dimpossible for either of us to remain much longer in the\u001b[K\r\u001b[16dhouse:  the fall of coals in the kitchen grate, the very\u001b[K\r\u001b[17dticking of the clock, filled us with alarms.\u001b[K\r\u001b[18d\u001b[K\u001b[31d\u001b[K\u001b[32d\u001b[K\u001b[33d\u001b[K\u001b[35;98H\u001b[1K \u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40mSpeed test\r\u001b[4dI\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m\u001b[35;110H"]
[699.354906, "o", "\r\u001b[4d\u001b[37m\u001b[40mI\u001b(B\u001b[0;7m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[39;49m\u001b[37m\u001b[40m"]
